[h1]After the End: Game over Scoreboard[/h1]

Just like in Crusader Kings II, this mod lets you see how far you've come — measured against the famous dynasties of After the End.

When your line finally ends, a new [b]Legacy Scoreboard[/b] button appears on the game over screen. It opens a reckoning: your dynasty's score, the house you surpassed, and the full ladder of the great houses of the post-Event world.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]What you'll see[/h2]

[list]
[*][b]Your score[/b], shown beside your own dynasty's coat of arms
[*][b]The house you surpassed[/b], with a short account of who they were and how they fell
[*][b]The full ladder[/b] — sixteen houses, from House Avondale's presidents of Chicago all the way up to House Talanque, Emperors of California
[*][b]Every house's history[/b] — hover any coat of arms to read it
[/list]

[h2]The houses[/h2]

Talanque, Jacaranda, Royall, Clinton, Sully, Abbas, Tlgunghung, Nokona, Mahonic, Castel, Pitchstone, Yoder, Tagötöka, Soady, Avondale — and one more, for those who fall short of them all.

Every coat of arms is the house's real heraldry, taken from After the End's own definitions.

[h2]How the score works[/h2]

Renown is a currency — it drops every time you buy a dynasty legacy, so ranking on the raw number would punish the players who actually spent it well. This mod reconstructs what your dynasty [i]earned[/i] across its whole history, counting every point ever spent as well as what's left in the bank.

The thresholds are the original CK2 scoreboard's, unchanged. Reaching the summit is meant to take a long and successful dynasty.

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Requirements[/h2]

[list]
[*][b]After the End[/b] — required
[*]Load this [b]after[/b] After the End in your playset
[/list]

[b]Compatibility:[/b] replaces the game over screen (window_succession_event.gui). It will conflict with any other mod that edits that same screen.

[b]Ironman / achievements:[/b] unaffected — this only changes what you see at the end.

[hr][/hr]

[i]All coat of arms artwork is generated from After the End's own definitions and belongs to that mod's authors.[/i]
